Unsupervised GA optimizer usage
===============================

1) Ensure you have a simulation entrypoint that exposes `build_sim(cycle_config)` (and optionally `run_visual`). The file is commonly named `main.py`.

2) Point the optimizer at that file in one of two ways:
   - Env var: `export TRAFFIC_SIM_MAIN="/full/path/to/your/main.py"`
   - CLI arg: `python ga_optimizer.py --sim-path \"/full/path/to/your/main.py\"`

3) Run the optimizer:
   `python ga_optimizer.py`
   (Defaults now run 200 generations with population 30; adjust via CLI flags.)

Notes:
- If your simulation `main.py` lives beside `ga_optimizer.py` or under this `Unsupervised` folder, it should be auto-discovered.
- If discovery still fails, set `TRAFFIC_SIM_MAIN` explicitly. A clear ImportError will be raised if `build_sim` cannot be found.

GUI visualization:
- A simple Tkinter visualizer is provided via `run_visual` in `main.py`; it shows queue lengths and signal phases.
- When `ga_optimizer.py` finishes, it will automatically call `run_visual` with the best config (requires a display).
